## Speed dating (1:1 WebRTC)

Video goes **browser-to-browser**, not through the R630 web servers. App servers only persist pairing + SDP/ICE in Postgres.

```bash
SPEEDDATING=false
# SPEED_DATE_STUN_URLS=stun:stun.l.google.com:19302,stun:stun1.l.google.com:19302
# SPEED_DATE_TURN_URLS=turn:192.168.222.202:3478?transport=udp
# SPEED_DATE_TURN_USERNAME=speeddate
# SPEED_DATE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=****
```

| Variable | Notes |
|----------|-------|
| `SPEEDDATING` | `true` → show the Speed Dating sidebar item (`fe/src/config/speedDatingEnv.js`). Any other value (or unset) hides it. Mirrored into the Vite FE bundle. Restart Vite / re-run FE build after changing. |
| `SPEED_DATE_STUN_URLS` | Comma-separated STUN URLs. Default is Google public STUN. |
| `SPEED_DATE_TURN_URLS` | Optional coturn relay on one R630 for guests behind strict NAT. Leave unset until coturn is running. |
| `SPEED_DATE_TURN_USERNAME` / `SPEED_DATE_TURN_CREDENTIAL` | Required with TURN URLs. Do not commit secrets. |

